---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "../../../components/common/Container.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Kumamoto City, Kumamoto Castle Main Tower｜Nishikino｜WORKS"
  description=""
>


<section class="relative h-[920px] overflow-hidden bg-[#f5f1ea]">

  <!-- Background -->

  <picture>

    <!-- Smartphone -->
    <source
      media="(max-width: 768px)"
      srcset="/images/kumamotocastle-mobile.jpg"
    />

    <!-- PC -->
    <img
      src="/images/kumamoto.jpg"
      alt="Kumamoto Castle Main Tower"
      class="work-hero absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover pointer-events-none select-none"
      draggable="false"
    />

  </picture>


  <!-- Content -->

  <div class="absolute inset-0 z-20 flex items-center">

    <Container>

      <div class="hero-content max-w-3xl">

        <!-- English -->

        <p
          class="mt-10 text-base tracking-[0.45em] text-[#f6e8c8]"
          style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;"
        >
          KUMAMOTO CASTLE MAIN TOWER
        </p>


        <!-- Title -->

        <h1
          class="mt-1 text-[43px] leading-[1.15] text-[#ffffff]"
          style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
        >
          熊本城天守閣
        </h1>


        <!-- Subtitle -->

        <p
          class="mt-6 text-xl text-[#ffffff]"
          style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
        >
          The great black castle of Kumamoto, also known as the Ginnan Castle.
        </p>

        <!-- Gold Divider -->

        <div class="mt-1">

          <img
            src="/images/gold-divider.png"
            alt=""
            class="w-[420px] h-auto select-none pointer-events-none"
            draggable="false"
          />

        </div>


        <!-- Summary -->

        <div class="mt-14 max-w-2xl">
        </div>


      </div>

    </Container>

  </div>


  <!-- Scroll -->

  <div class="absolute bottom-16 right-12 z-30 flex flex-col items-center">

    <div class="h-20 w-px bg-white/70"></div>

    <span class="mt-4 text-base tracking-[0.45em] text-white">
      SCROLL
    </span>

  </div>

</section>


<section class="relative bg-[#f8f6f2] overflow-hidden works-detail">

  <!-- Washi Background -->

  <img
    src="/images/washi-bg.png"
    alt=""
    class="absolute right-0 top-0 h-full w-full opacity-[0.3] pointer-events-none select-none -z-0"
  />


  <Container class="py-32 relative z-10">



    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">

      <div class="flex items-center gap-6">

        <span class="h-px w-24 bg-[#caa14d]"></span>

        <p
          class="text-base tracking-[0.45em] text-[#9a8358]"
          style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;"
        >
          OVERVIEW
        </p>

      </div>


      <h2
        class="mt-8 text-3xl text-[#2b2724]"
        style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
      >
        Overview
      </h2>


      <p
        class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-base leading-10 text-[#55504a]"
        style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
      >
        Kumamoto Castle, a prominent early modern Japanese castle built in present-day Kumamoto City, Kumamoto Prefecture, is one of Japan's most renowned castles. It was constructed under the direction of Kato Kiyomasa, with construction beginning around 1601 during the Keicho era.<br>
        The castle developed into one of the largest castle complexes in western Japan, featuring vast baileys, imposing stone walls, and numerous towers and gates.<br>
        Its distinctive stone walls, known as <em>Musha-gaeshi</em>, curve outward at the base and become increasingly steep toward the top. Together with its imposing black main tower, they have become defining symbols of Kumamoto Castle, which is also counted among Japan's Three Great Castles.
      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-6xl">
    </div>


    <div class="mx-auto mt-24 grid max-w-6xl gap-16 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_360px]">

      <!-- Left -->

      <div>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-5">

          <span class="h-px w-20 bg-[#caa14d]"></span>

          <p
            class="text-base tracking-[0.4em] text-[#9a8358]"
            style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;"
          >
            HISTORY
          </p>

        </div>


        <h2
          class="mt-8 text-3xl text-[#2b2724]"
          style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
        >
          About Kumamoto Castle and Its Main Tower
        </h2>


        <p
          class="mt-10 text-base leading-10 text-[#4f4944]"
          style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
        >

          Kumamoto Castle is an early modern Japanese castle built from the Azuchi-Momoyama period through the beginning of the Edo period.
          Construction was carried out under the direction of Kato Kiyomasa from around 1601, during the Keicho era.
          Kiyomasa was highly skilled in flood control and civil engineering, and Kumamoto Castle incorporated sophisticated defensive and practical engineering techniques.

          <br><br>

          One of its most distinctive features is the unique curved stone walls known as <em>Musha-gaeshi</em>, designed to prevent enemy forces from scaling the castle.
          The walls are relatively gentle at the bottom and become increasingly steep toward the top.
          This design was not merely aesthetically striking but also provided a high level of defensive capability, making it one of Kumamoto Castle's defining architectural characteristics.

          <br><br>

          The original main tower complex consisted of a large main tower and a smaller main tower, forming a connected watchtower-style design.
          Its imposing appearance featured black lacquered weatherboards, white plaster walls, and substantial gable decorations,
          creating a dignified exterior characteristic of early modern Japanese castles.

          <br><br>

          <br><br>

          From the Meiji period onward, Kumamoto Castle entered a major turning point in its history.
          During the Satsuma Rebellion of 1877, the castle became an important government military stronghold and the site of a prolonged siege.
          Many structures, including the main palace and castle towers, were destroyed by fire during this period.
          However, portions of the original castle, including its massive stone walls, towers, and gates, survived and continued to be preserved as an enduring symbol of Kumamoto.

          <br><br>

          In the modern era, efforts to preserve and restore Kumamoto Castle as a cultural property progressed.
          In 1960, the main tower was reconstructed using reinforced concrete.
          Today, together with restored structures and surviving important cultural properties, Kumamoto Castle remains one of Japan's most representative historic castle complexes and continues to attract visitors from around the world.

          <br><br>

          However, the Kumamoto Earthquake of April 2016 caused extensive damage to the castle.
          The main tower, stone walls, towers, and important cultural properties were among the structures severely affected.
          Approximately 20 percent of the castle's stone walls collapsed, causing significant damage to a castle complex with more than 400 years of history.

          <br><br>

          Following the earthquake, large-scale restoration work began, with Kumamoto Castle serving as a symbol of recovery.
          After seismic reinforcement and interior renovations, the main tower reopened for special public viewing in 2020.
          Restoration and preservation work continues today, particularly on the stone walls and groups of towers, with the aim of protecting the castle's cultural heritage for future generations.

          <br><br>

          Kumamoto Castle also continues to face the challenge of preparing for natural disasters.
          On July 28, 2026, a magnitude 7.1 earthquake occurred with its epicenter in the Kumamoto region of Kumamoto Prefecture.
          The event once again drew attention to the importance of disaster preparedness and preservation efforts to pass historic structures on to future generations.

          <br><br>

          With more than 400 years of history, Kumamoto Castle has endured warfare, modernization, and repeated natural disasters.
          It continues to be preserved and passed on to the future as one of the defining cultural landmarks of Kumamoto.

          <br><br>

          For this work, I recreated the Kumamoto Castle main tower as it appears following its restoration, using on-site photographs and historical and architectural references as the basis for a Japanese-style Minecraft build.

          <br><br>

          Rather than focusing solely on the main tower, I also considered the wider structure and landscape of Kumamoto Castle so that the project could eventually be expanded into a recreation of the entire castle complex, including the Honmaru Palace, Uto Tower, other towers, gates, and stone walls.

        </p>

      </div>


      <!-- DATA -->

      <aside class="relative">

        <div
          class="rounded-[2rem] border border-[#e2d8cb] bg-[#fffdfa] p-10 shadow-[0_20px_60px_rgba(0,0,0,.07)]"
        >

          <p
            class="text-base tracking-[0.4em] text-[#a68b64]"
            style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;"
          >
            DATA
          </p>


          <div class="mt-10 space-y-8">

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Work</p>
              <p class="text-base">Kumamoto Castle Main Tower</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Category</p>
              <p class="text-base">Japanese Castle・Main Tower</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Period</p>
              <p class="text-base">Early Edo Period</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Location</p>
              <p class="text-base">
                1-1 Honmaru, Chuo Ward, Kumamoto City, Kumamoto 860-0002, Japan
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Construction</p>
              <p class="text-base">Around 1601 (Keicho 6)</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Builder</p>
              <p class="text-base">Kato Kiyomasa</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Style</p>
              <p class="text-base">Combined Watchtower-Style Main Tower</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Software</p>
              <p class="text-base">Minecraft Java Edition 1.21.5</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Work Type</p>
              <p class="text-base">Japanese Architecture・Reconstruction</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <p class="text-base text-[#8c8378]">Status</p>
              <p class="text-base">Completed</p>
            </div>

          </div>

        </div>

      </aside>

    </div>


    <div class="mx-auto mt-32 max-w-6xl">

      <div class="flex items-center gap-5">

        <span class="h-px w-20 bg-[#caa14d]"></span>

        <p
          class="text-base tracking-[0.45em] text-[#a58c65]"
          style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;"
        >
          GALLERY
        </p>

      </div>


      <h2
        class="mt-6 text-4xl"
        style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
      >
        Gallery
      </h2>


      <div class="gallery mt-12">

        <div class="gallery-frame">
          <img
            src="/images/kumamoto.jpg"
            alt="Kumamoto Castle Main Tower"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="gallery-frame">
          <img
            src="/images/kumamoto1.png"
            alt="Kumamoto Castle Main Tower"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="gallery-frame">
          <img
            src="/images/kumamoto2.png"
            alt="Kumamoto Castle Main Tower"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="gallery-frame">
          <img
            src="/images/kumamoto3.png"
            alt="Kumamoto Castle Main Tower"
          />
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>


    <div class="mt-24 flex flex-wrap gap-4">

      <a
        href="/en/works/"
        class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-[#d7c8b3] bg-white px-8 py-4 text-base transition hover:bg-[#2b2724] hover:text-white"
      >
        ← Back to Works
      </a>


      <a
        href="https://x.com/nishikinolab/status/1950147940971892883/photo/1"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-[#d7c8b3] bg-white px-8 py-4 text-base transition hover:bg-[#2b2724] hover:text-white"
      >
        View More →
      </a>


      <a
        href="https://youtube.com/shorts/QzWMzN91y7E"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-[#d7c8b3] bg-white px-8 py-4 text-base transition hover:bg-[#2b2724] hover:text-white"
      >
        Watch Video →
      </a>


      <div class="mt-32 text-center w-full">

        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-5">

          <span class="h-px w-16 bg-[#caa14d]"></span>

          <p
            class="text-base tracking-[0.45em] text-[#a58c65]"
            style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;"
          >
            SHARE
          </p>

          <span class="h-px w-16 bg-[#caa14d]"></span>

        </div>


        <h2
          class="mt-6 text-3xl text-[#2b2724]"
          style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
        >
          Share This Work
        </h2>


        <div class="mt-8 flex justify-center gap-4 flex-wrap">

          <!-- X -->

          <a
            href="#"
            id="x-share"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="rounded-full border border-[#d7c8b3] bg-white px-7 py-3 text-base hover:bg-[#2b2724] hover:text-white"
          >
            X
          </a>


          <!-- Instagram -->

          <button
            type="button"
            id="instagram-share"
            class="rounded-full border border-[#d7c8b3] bg-white px-7 py-3 text-base hover:bg-[#2b2724] hover:text-white"
          >
            Instagram
          </button>


          <!-- Copy -->

          <button
            type="button"
            id="copy-url"
            class="rounded-full border border-[#d7c8b3] bg-white px-7 py-3 text-base hover:bg-[#2b2724] hover:text-white"
          >
            Copy URL
          </button>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </Container>

</section>


<script>

const sharePhrases = [
  "Found this.",
  "I kind of like this.",
  "Look at this.",
  "Found something interesting.",
  "Found something like this.",
  "Have you seen this?",
  "Found something.",
  "Came across this.",
  "Found something worth checking out."
];


const randomPhrase =
  sharePhrases[
    Math.floor(Math.random() * sharePhrases.length)
  ];


const pageUrl =
  "https://www.nishikinolab.net/en/kumamotocastle/";


const shareText =
  `${randomPhrase} Minecraft KUMAMOTO CASTLE MAIN TOWER | WORKS`;


const xShare =
  document.getElementById("x-share");


if (xShare) {

  xShare.setAttribute(
    "href",
    `https://x.com/intent/post?text=${encodeURIComponent(shareText)}&url=${encodeURIComponent(pageUrl)}`
  );

}


const copyButton =
  document.getElementById("copy-url");


const instagramButton =
  document.getElementById("instagram-share");


copyButton?.addEventListener("click", async () => {

  try {

    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(pageUrl);

    if (copyButton) {

      copyButton.textContent = "Copied";

      setTimeout(() => {

        copyButton.textContent = "Copy URL";

      }, 2000);

    }

  } catch (error) {

    console.error(error);

  }

});


instagramButton?.addEventListener("click", () => {

  const dialog =
    document.createElement("div");


  dialog.innerHTML = `

    <div
      id="instagram-share-overlay"
      style="
        position:fixed;
        inset:0;
        z-index:9999;
        display:flex;
        align-items:center;
        justify-content:center;
        padding:24px;
        background:rgba(43,39,36,.55);
        backdrop-filter:blur(6px);
      "
    >

      <div
        style="
          width:100%;
          max-width:420px;
          padding:36px;
          border:1px solid #e2d8cb;
          border-radius:28px;
          background:#fffdfa;
          box-shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.18);
          text-align:center;
        "
      >

        <p
          style="
            margin:0;
            font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;
            font-size:14px;
            letter-spacing:.35em;
            color:#a58c65;
          "
        >
          SHARE
        </p>


        <h3
          style="
            margin:14px 0 0;
            font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;
            font-size:24px;
            color:#2b2724;
            font-weight:400;
          "
        >
          Share on Instagram
        </h3>


        <p
          style="
            margin:20px 0 0;
            font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;
            font-size:14px;
            line-height:2;
            color:#625a52;
          "
        >
          The URL of this work page will be copied<br>
          and Instagram will be opened.
        </p>


        <button
          id="instagram-open"
          type="button"
          style="
            width:100%;
            margin-top:28px;
            padding:14px 20px;
            border:1px solid #d7c8b3;
            border-radius:999px;
            background:#2b2724;
            color:#fff;
            font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;
            font-size:15px;
            cursor:pointer;
          "
        >
          Copy URL & Open Instagram
        </button>


        <button
          id="instagram-cancel"
          type="button"
          style="
            width:100%;
            margin-top:10px;
            padding:12px 20px;
            border:0;
            background:transparent;
            color:#8c8378;
            font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;
            font-size:14px;
            cursor:pointer;
          "
        >
          Cancel
        </button>

      </div>

    </div>

  `;


  document.body.appendChild(dialog);


  const overlay =
    document.getElementById(
      "instagram-share-overlay"
    );


  const openButton =
    document.getElementById(
      "instagram-open"
    );


  const cancelButton =
    document.getElementById(
      "instagram-cancel"
    );


  openButton?.addEventListener(
    "click",
    async () => {

      try {

        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(
          pageUrl
        );

      } catch (error) {

        console.error(error);

      }


      window.open(
        "https://www.instagram.com/",
        "_blank",
        "noopener,noreferrer"
      );


      overlay?.remove();

    }
  );


  cancelButton?.addEventListener(
    "click",
    () => {

      overlay?.remove();

    }
  );


  overlay?.addEventListener(
    "click",
    (event) => {

      if (event.target === overlay) {

        overlay.remove();

      }

    }
  );

});


</script>


<style>

.work-hero {

  animation:
    heroFloat 12s ease-in-out infinite;

  transform-origin:
    center;

}


@keyframes heroFloat {

  0% {

    transform:
      scale(1.03)
      translateY(0);

  }

  50% {

    transform:
      scale(1.06)
      translateY(-18px);

  }

  100% {

    transform:
      scale(1.03)
      translateY(0);

  }

}


section {

  position:
    relative;

}


section::before {

  content:
    "";

  position:
    absolute;

  left:
    0;

  top:
    0;

  width:
    100%;

  height:
    100%;

  pointer-events:
    none;

  background-image:

    radial-gradient(
      circle at 8% 10%,
      rgba(205,175,98,.08),
      transparent 18%
    ),

    radial-gradient(
      circle at 92% 82%,
      rgba(205,175,98,.06),
      transparent 22%
    );

}


aside {

  position:
    sticky;

  top:
    120px;

  height:
    max-content;

}


a {

  transition:
    .35s;

}



.gallery-frame {

  position:
    relative;

  padding:
    2px;

  border-radius:
    1.25rem;

  background:

    linear-gradient(
      to right,
      transparent 0%,
      rgba(253, 164, 175, 0.65) 25%,
      rgba(252, 211, 77, 0.65) 50%,
      rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.65) 75%,
      transparent 100%
    );

  overflow:
    hidden;

}


.gallery-frame img {

  display:
    block;

  width:
    100%;

  height:
    auto;

  border-radius:
    calc(1.25rem - 2px);

  background:
    #f8f6f2;

}


.gallery-frame:hover {

  background:

    linear-gradient(
      to right,
      transparent 0%,
      rgba(253, 164, 175, 0.9) 25%,
      rgba(252, 211, 77, 0.9) 50%,
      rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.9) 75%,
      transparent 100%
    );

}


@media (max-width:1100px) {

  section {

    overflow:
      hidden;

  }


}


@media (max-width:900px) {

  aside {

    position:
      relative;

    top:
      auto;

  }


}


@media (max-width:768px) {

  section:first-child {

    height:
      760px;

  }

  h1 {

    font-size:
      44px !important;

    line-height:
      1.15;

  }

  h2 {

    font-size:
      32px !important;

  }

  /*
   * Hero animationは停止しない。
   * PC・スマホとも同じアニメーションを維持。
   */

  .gallery-frame {

    border-radius:
      1rem;

  }

  .gallery-frame img {

    border-radius:
      calc(1rem - 2px);

  }

}

</style>


</Layout>